### ============================================================================
### Practical 5: MongoDB & Mongoose Task Management REST API Test Suite
### Compatible with Visual Studio Code REST Client extension (Humao.rest-client)
### Base URL: http://localhost:5000
### ============================================================================

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000

### 1. GET all tasks (Expected Status: 200 OK)
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Accept: application/json

###

### 2. POST a valid task with all fields (Expected Status: 201 Created)
# @name createTask
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Complete Practical 5",
  "description": "Integrate MongoDB and Mongoose with Express",
  "completed": false,
  "priority": "high"
}

###

### 3. POST without a title (Expected Status: 400 Bad Request - Validation Error)
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "description": "Missing title field",
  "completed": false,
  "priority": "medium"
}

###

### 4. POST with a blank/empty title (Expected Status: 400 Bad Request - Validation Error)
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "   ",
  "description": "Whitespace only title",
  "completed": false
}

###

### 5. POST with invalid priority 'urgent' (Expected Status: 400 Bad Request - Enum Validation)
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Invalid Priority Task",
  "description": "Priority 'urgent' is not in enum [low, medium, high]",
  "priority": "urgent"
}

###

### 6. POST without completed or priority to test schema defaults (Expected Status: 201 Created)
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Default Schema Values Task",
  "description": "completed should default to false, priority to medium"
}

###

### 7. GET specific task by MongoDB ObjectId (Supplementary Endpoint - Expected Status: 200 OK)
# Replace {{taskId}} with an actual ObjectId returned from POST /tasks
@taskId = {{createTask.response.body._id}}
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{taskId}}
Accept: application/json

###

### 8. GET task with nonexistent valid ObjectId (Expected Status: 404 Not Found)
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks/507f1f77bcf86cd799439011
Accept: application/json

###

### 9. GET task with malformed/invalid ObjectId (Expected Status: 400 Bad Request)
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks/invalid-object-id
Accept: application/json

###

### 10. PUT an existing task by MongoDB ObjectId (Expected Status: 200 OK)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{taskId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "completed": true,
  "priority": "low",
  "description": "Updated task description and marked completed"
}

###

### 11. PUT a nonexistent task by valid ObjectId (Expected Status: 404 Not Found)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/tasks/507f1f77bcf86cd799439011
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Non-existent Task"
}

###

### 12. PUT with an invalid/malformed ObjectId (Expected Status: 400 Bad Request)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/tasks/invalid-id-123
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Invalid ID Task"
}

###

### 13. DELETE an existing task by MongoDB ObjectId (Expected Status: 200 OK)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{taskId}}
Accept: application/json

###

### 14. DELETE a nonexistent task by valid ObjectId (Expected Status: 404 Not Found)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/tasks/507f1f77bcf86cd799439011
Accept: application/json

###

### 15. POST without application/json Content-Type (Expected Status: 400 Bad Request)
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Content-Type: text/plain

title=No+Json+Header

###

### 16. Request an undefined route (Expected Status: 404 Not Found)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/non-existent-endpoint
Accept: application/json
